BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature TO Tour: Trees Around Beaches Branch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T143000
UID:6a29c1532ea730c17ab5ed59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Beaches Library is nestled next to Kew Gardens\, a vibrant hom
 e to many species of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff 
 for a guided neighbourhood tour through Kew Gardens\, where you’ll learn
  to identify different tree species and discover fascinating facts about t
 heir cultural and ecological significance.\nPlease note:\nChildren under 1
 2 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. There may be uneven\, unpaved
  surfaces along the route. Please prepare accordingly for this outdoor tou
 r (comfortable footwear\, sunscreen). This tour takes place rain or shine.
  In the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified o
 f an alternative date.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29c1532ea730c17ab5ed59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
